Just the other day I saw someone playing NetHack3, and it inspired
me to have a go at compiling it up. So I go to our old news archive
and grab all the sources. Then I apply all the patches. THEN I try
to compile it. And here is the rub...

At patchlevel 4 Makefile.src (i.e. the Makefile from the src
subdirectory) has circular dependencies, eg:

	makedefs depends on objects.o
	objects.o depends on decl.h
	decl.h depends on onames.h
	onames.h depends on makedefs

To compile objects.c I need onames.h, but I can't create onames.h
until I have compiled objects.c. So I am stuck.

I assume this was introduced by one of the patches, or else noone
would have been able to get off the ground and someone would have
mentioned it here before, I have not checked yet.

I think it should be fixed as it is a pain to compile NetHack, then
apply a patch then recompile, etc, the four times needed.

